  "name": "Ba'al (Canaanite god worshipped by the Israelites)",
  "title": "Canaanite fertility god and rival of Yahweh",
  "era": "divided-kingdom",
  "summary": "Ba'al was the foremost Canaanite god of fertility and storms, widely worshipped in the ancient Near East. The Israelites repeatedly fell into Ba'al worship, which posed the most persistent threat to the worship of the one true God, Yahweh. The prophets, especially Elijah and Hosea, fought fiercely against the Ba'al cult and called the people back to covenant faithfulness.",
